<title>GERMANY: BASF says tapes unit to post 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>BASF says tapes unit to post 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>BASF Magnetics GmbH, a unit of German chemical group BASF AG, is expected to post a 1996 operating loss of about 20 million marks ($13.3 million), BASF Chief Financial Officer Max Dietrich Kley said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Kley told a news conference that the unit has faced severe price pressures.</p>
<p>&quot;Prices have fallen more rapidly than we were able to implement cost-cutting measures,&quot; Kley said.</p>
<p>BASF is in the process of selling the unprofitable unit, one of the world's best-known cassette tape makers, to Turkey's RAK Holding A.S..</p>
<p>Negotiations with RAK would continue on the basis of a letter of intent already signed while the Potash Corp. talks were already at an advanced stage, BASF said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.507 German Marks)</p>
